From 374750c61ffe20cd5a698d8b560c5a85d9dd8112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:35:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 37/75] PlaitOS: Section 3 fixes from review

- Battery percentage: keep GrapheneOS's Quick Settings header (always the
  percentage plus the time-left estimate, shade-blur text color) and lock
  screen (percentage while charging or whenever it is shown at all); the
  PlaitOS setting now controls the home status bar only, so unset stays stock
- Bluetooth battery: read mConnectedDevices under its lock; it is
  @GuardedBy and changed from Bluetooth callbacks, so a disconnect between
  isEmpty() and get(0) could crash SystemUI
- Double tap to sleep: the panel detector only acts on the lock screen; it
  also fired on empty space in the pulled-down shade (the status bar strip
  is handled by QQSGestureListener)
- Brightness control: put getDisplayWidth()'s @Override/@Deprecated back on
  it (the inserted methods had split them off; build error)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
